course: dictionary
lesson: 5433
title: Lakota: a people and a language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lakota is a name for a people, so it starts with a capital letter. «On the Great Plains nations such as the Lakota followed huge herds of bison» tells you the Lakota lived on the wide, flat plains and hunted bison there.
explain: Lakota can also name a language. Look at the words around it. In «the Lakota people», Lakota describes the people, so it works like an adjective. In «the Lakota» on its own, it names the whole group, so it works like a noun.
explain: Some words can be different parts of speech, so always check the context. Ask yourself: is this word naming something, or describing something? Then use the clues in the sentence to decide.
fact: The Lakota are a people of the Great Plains, part of the Sioux nation.
fact: Lakota is also the name of their language.
fact: Horses came back to the Americas with the Spanish in the 1500s, and the Lakota became expert riders.
fact: Sitting Bull and Crazy Horse are famous Lakota leaders.
fact: Many Lakota people today work to keep their language alive.
exercise: «On the Great Plains nations such as the Lakota followed huge herds of bison.» Where did the Lakota live? | *On the Great Plains | In the Arctic snow | On small Greek islands | In the deserts of Spain
exercise: «After the Spanish brought horses they became expert riders.» What does expert mean? | Very slow | Very new | *Very skilled | Very frightened
exercise: Many Lakota people today work to keep their language alive. What is the Lakota language? | A river in the Black Hills | A type of horse | *The language of the Lakota people | A kind of buffalo
test: «Native peoples of North America were many nations with hundreds of languages, such as the Cherokee, Navajo, Lakota, Haudenosaunee, Inuit and Cree.» What kind of group is the Lakota? | *A people, part of the Sioux nation | A herd of bison | A country with its own king | A city in Norway
test: Name one famous Lakota leader from the lessons. | Black Hills | Little Bighorn | *Crazy Horse | Spanish
exam: «Think of how different Norway, Spain and Greece are: the Inuit of the Arctic, the Lakota of the Plains and the Pueblo peoples of the desert were just as different.» What is the main idea? | Norway, Spain and Greece are the same | Deserts are cold | All peoples live in the same way | *Peoples of North America were very different from one another
